==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
-

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Given the high pushing power of Star Peng and Ursa Major, it's highly recommended to bring [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] or, if owned, [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]], alongside good Long Distance attackers like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]. Despite having only two Zombie enemies, the presence of the powerful Zapies means that Holy Blast is recommended to cleave through their health. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] or [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]] are recommended against them; the former can tank a hit from a Zapy to give your other units more breathing room (and becomes especially valuable if his Immune to Warp talent is unlocked), while the latter can chip at their health while Cursing them so that they don't clog up your deploy limit with Warped units.

While locked behind an utterly brutal Revenge Stage, [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]] makes this level significantly easier by preventing the Star Pengs and Zapies from warping your units, in addition to being able to wear down Ursa Major.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Deathshund seems nasty on paper with Star Pengs backing it, but the short stage length and the fact it burrows (much like all other Zombies here) allows the player to stack up some attackers and sneak past it, destroying the enemy base before it could even surface. [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] notably helps to hold the front while the likes of [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] melt through the Star Pengs, tearing the base into pieces shortly after.

